      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CARLANDO (7) has the clearest winning case after returning with a nose second at this track in Open grade, and the move into a BM60 looks a strong piece of placement. He is already a track-and-trip winner, has missed a place only once in five starts, and his 950m record gives him the right profile second-up. DO A LITTLE DANCE (6) brings winning form after scoring at this track in a Mdn and then at Cooktown in a BM50, though this is a harder meeting and a sharper grade test. The weight relief from last start helps him carry that form across. GOLDEN OCTAVIAN (5) was doing his best work late when fourth here first-up in a BM65 and is better suited with that run behind him, but his recent winless patch keeps him more to the each-way side. MACHINE HEAD (1) resumes off a comfortable Cairns trial and has placed four times from six starts at this track and distance, yet he has to turn that readiness into a sharper race-day finish than he showed at the end of last preparation.",
